# 🧬 Bulk RNA-seq Analysis Pipeline with Snakemake

[![Snakemake](https://img.shields.io/badge/snakemake-≥7.0-brightgreen.svg)](https://snakemake.github.io)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
[![Nextflow](https://img.shields.io/badge/nextflow-Not%20today-blue)](https://snakemake.github.io)

> **A production-ready, reproducible bulk RNA-seq pipeline from FASTQ to biological insights**

## 🎯 What This Pipeline Does

| Step | Tool | Output |
|------|------|--------|
| Quality Control | FastQC + MultiQC | Interactive HTML reports |
| Read Alignment | STAR (2-pass mode) | Sorted BAM files |
| Quantification | featureCounts | Gene-level count matrix |
| Differential Expression | DESeq2 + apeglm | Log2FC, padj, normalized counts |
| Functional Enrichment | clusterProfiler | GO/KEGG pathways |
| Visualization | ggplot2 / pheatmap | Volcano plots, heatmaps, PCA |

**End-to-end automation**: One command goes from `data/raw/*.fastq.gz` to `results/report.html`

## 🚀 Quick Start

### Prerequisites
```bash
# Install conda (if not already)
# Then install Snakemake
conda create -n snakemake -c bioconda snakemake
conda activate snakemake
```
### Run the pipeline
```bash
# Dry run to see what will happen
snakemake -n

# Run full pipeline with test data
snakemake --cores 4 --use-conda

# Generate workflow DAG (dependency graph)
snakemake --dag | dot -Tpng > workflow.png
```